115-## [2] ACTIVATION CONDITIONS
116-
117-Activate this overlay when one or more of the following apply:
118-- agent behavior must be compared across versions, prompts, tools, or workflows
119-- the system will operate in dynamic or live environments
120-- regression detection materially matters
121-- production or canary monitoring materially matters
122:- latency, cost, or resource consumption materially matter
123-- safety, compliance, or policy adherence materially matter
124:- drift risk is non-trivial
125-- trajectory quality matters, not just final answer quality
126-- agent behavior must be benchmarked before release
127-- qualitative outputs require structured review beyond exact-match metrics
128-- multi-agent or tool-using behavior must be assessed as a system
129-- release gating or rollout decisions depend on measurable quality criteria
130-- prompt-stack rewrites, variant changes, or overlay changes may alter behavior materially
131-- long-running optimization or continuous improvement loops need reliable signal
132-- a high-stakes deployment requires ongoing assurance rather than one-time testing
133-
134-Do not activate when:
135-- the task is trivial and one-shot
136-- the current request is fully local and does not justify formal evaluation
137-- monitoring overhead clearly exceeds decision value
138-- a simple local verification step is enough
139-- no comparison, rollout, or long-term quality signal is needed
140-- the system is exploratory and the user only wants a provisional draft without evaluation discipline
141-
142-Activation rule:
143-- activate on expected quality-control leverage, not on instrumentation aesthetics
144-- when activated, keep evaluation bounded and contract-aware
145-- deactivate once incremental monitoring or evaluation no longer changes decisions materially
