216-## [4] EVALUATION-MONITORING DECISION MODEL
217-
218-When this overlay is active, evaluation and monitoring discipline should follow this logic:
219-
220-`Clarify Quality Objective -> Define Contract Surface -> Select Evaluation Scope -> Select Metric Set -> Select Evidence and Observation Method -> Execute / Observe -> Score / Judge / Compare -> Detect Regressions, Drift, or Anomalies -> Report -> Escalate / Gate / Improve / Continue Monitoring`
221-
222-Decision rules:
223-- do not measure before defining what quality must mean for this system
224-- do not compare variants without a stable evaluation surface
225:- do not deploy monitoring without knowing what thresholds matter
226-- do not collect metrics with no intended decision use
227-- do not treat high visibility as high signal
228-- do not use one metric as a proxy for all quality dimensions
229-- do not synthesize monitoring outputs into false confidence when coverage is weak
230-- do not approve a prompt rewrite merely because style improved
231-
