437-## [7] CONTRACT-FIRST EVALUATION
438-
439-Evaluation should be tied to explicit contracts whenever possible.
440-
441-A contract may define:
442-- expected deliverable
443-- required sections or schema
444-- allowed scope
445-- forbidden scope
446-- required evidence behavior
447-- required risk behavior
448-- approval boundary
449-- acceptance criteria
450-- stop conditions
451-- downgrade or propose-only expectations
452-
453-Contract-first rules:
454-- evaluate against what was actually promised
455-- do not judge a system for not doing what was outside the contract
456-- if the contract is weak, strengthen the contract before multiplying metrics
457-- high-stakes systems should prefer verifiable deliverables over vague quality aspirations
458-
459-Contract rule:
