507-### 8.4 Eval set anti-patterns
508-
509-Avoid:
510-- only happy-path cases
511-- only toy tasks
512:- only easy deterministic tasks
513-- duplicated near-identical cases that inflate confidence
514-- benchmark cases that do not map to real deployment risk
515-- cases with unclear scoring semantics
516-- prompt-only comparisons on tasks that do not exercise the changed behavior
517-
518-Eval set rule:
519-- represent the real quality surface
520-- not just the easiest measurable subset
521-
522-### 8.5 Dedicated harness and mock-tool policy
523-
524-When agentic workflows depend on tools or external state:
525-- prefer mock tools or a dedicated safe test harness for repeatable evaluation
526:- assert tool-call parameters, partial-state handling, and final answer elements separately when possible
527:- distinguish deterministic acceptance checks from rubric or judge-style scoring
528-- when coding-agent quality is being compared, define whether verification-running expectations are required, optional, or unavailable before claiming repo-scale proof
529-
530-### 8.6 Benchmark registry and replay program
531-
532-When evaluation is versioned or release-sensitive, preserve:
533-- scenario identity
534-- task family
535-- cohort or environment boundary
536-- expected packet floor
537-- expected route class
538-- expected failure class
539-- replay support status
540-
541-Registry rule:
542-- a benchmark registry should define what is being compared before scores are discussed
543-- replay coverage should remain visible when benchmark conclusions depend on process quality rather than only output quality
544-
545-### 8.7 Executable benchmark and replay state
546-
547-When benchmark or replay claims become release-relevant, preserve:
548-- benchmark execution state
549-- replay execution state
550-- executed cohort boundary
551-- verdict reproducibility note
552-- unexecuted or partially executed slices
553-
554-Execution-state rule:
555-- a benchmark registry is not a benchmark execution result
556-- a replay-ready scenario list is not a replay verdict
