674-## [12] TRAJECTORY EVALUATION
675-
676-Trajectory evaluation is necessary when agentic workflows matter.
677-
678-Trajectory dimensions may include:
679-- step count
680-- branch count
681-- unnecessary detours
682:- tool-call fit
683-- retrieval discipline
684-- handoff integrity
685-- checkpoint quality
686-- recovery quality
687-- contract-preserving behavior
688-- stop-condition discipline
689-- stagnation pressure or repeated low-value loops
690-
691-Trajectory rules:
692-- compare the actual path against an ideal or acceptable path class
693-- do not require one exact path when multiple safe paths exist
694:- penalize avoidable inefficiency when it materially affects cost, latency, or reliability
695-- reward safe recovery over brittle one-shot perfection when appropriate
696-- distinguish good final answers achieved wastefully from good final answers achieved efficiently
697-
698-Trajectory anti-patterns:
699-- scoring only the final answer when the path itself creates operational risk
700-- over-penalizing harmless path variation
701-- assuming the shortest path is always the best path
702-- ignoring repeated low-value loops
703-
704-### 12.1 Safe trajectory artifact schema
705-
706-When trajectory inspection matters, preserve compact artifacts such as:
707-- `step_intent`
708:- `selected_action`
709-- `observation_summary`
710-- `branch_decision`
711-- `recovery_event`
712-- `stop_reason`
713-- `observed_packet_emission`
714-- `omission_findings`
715-- `replay_verdict`
716-
717-Artifact rule:
718-- do not require raw hidden chain-of-thought when compact auditable trajectory state is enough
719-- evaluate the observable path quality, not private reasoning verbosity
720-
721-### 12.2 Quality iteration checkpoint schema
722-
723-When an intermediate judgment should change the next route rather than merely score the last route, preserve compact artifacts such as:
724-- `quality_surface`
725-- `current_result_state`
726-- `baseline_reference`
727-- `gate_decision`
728-- `next_route`
729-- `fallback_route`
730-- `stop_trigger`
731-
732-Checkpoint rule:
733-- keep the checkpoint tied to a real continue / reroute / stop decision
734-- do not turn an iteration gate into a delayed postmortem
