778-### 13.3 Monitoring rule
779-
780-Monitoring should be:
781-- continuous enough to catch meaningful degradation
782-- bounded enough to avoid metric overload
783:- linked to thresholds and decisions
784-- separated into operational vs diagnostic views when helpful
785-
786-Monitoring anti-patterns:
787-- instrumenting everything without a decision model
788-- no distinction between transient noise and meaningful degradation
789:- dashboards with no thresholds, owners, or actions
790-- monitoring that cannot trigger any response
