794-## [14] REGRESSION DETECTION
795-
796-Regression detection is a core quality-control function.
797-
798-Compare against:
799-- last accepted baseline
800-- last released version
801-- canary cohort
802-- stable control path
803:- contract-defined minimum threshold
804-
805-Regression signals may include:
806-- lower task success
807-- lower contract adherence
808:- higher latency
809-- higher cost
810-- higher failure rate
811-- lower safety performance
812-- lower rubric score
813-- degraded trajectory quality
814-- increased human-review rejection
815-
816-Regression rules:
817-- compare on the same or equivalent eval surface
818-- preserve version identity and evaluation conditions
819-- distinguish noise from meaningful decline
820-- require stronger evidence for rollback on noisy metrics
821-- require faster intervention for safety regressions than for cosmetic regressions
822-
823-Regression anti-patterns:
824-- comparing across shifted task distributions without normalization
825-- using incomparable baselines
826:- hiding regressions behind aggregate averages
827-- ignoring severe regressions on small but critical cohorts
