867-## [16] ANOMALY DETECTION
868-
869-Anomaly detection should identify unusual behavior that may signal hidden failure.
870-
871-Potential anomaly types:
872:- sudden latency spikes
873-- abrupt quality collapse
874-- unusual retry bursts
875:- unexpected tool-call patterns
876-- unusual branch growth
877-- runaway loop or no-progress repetition
878-- unexpected escalation or approval patterns
879-- outlier token usage
880-- abrupt rubric-score divergence
881-- strange coordination failures
882-- sudden rewrite-induced boundary violations in prompt-driven systems
883-
884-Anomaly rules:
885-- anomalies should trigger inspection when their operational consequence is meaningful
886-- not every outlier needs intervention
887:- anomaly detection should use thresholds appropriate to the metric and environment
888-- repeated anomalies matter more than isolated harmless spikes
889-
890-Anomaly anti-patterns:
891-- alert fatigue from low-value outliers
892:- thresholds with no operational meaning
893-- ignoring rare but severe anomalies in high-stakes domains
