1204-
1205:Interaction rule:
1206:- preserve ownership boundaries
1207-- evaluation may assess any owned surface
1208:- it does not inherit control ownership over that surface
1209-
1210-### 25.7 Operational artifact governance
1211-
1212:When evaluation is being used to support repeated execution, promotion, or drift review:
1213-- distinguish packet presence from linked operational evidence
1214-- preserve stable identifiers such as `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` across benchmark, replay, adaptation, release, and telemetry artifacts
1215:- for guide-reflection maintenance, keep `BR-00 / runtime owner integrity` and `BR-19 / benchmark-loop adequacy` at document-level benchmark while the active runtime bundle directly exposes the owner boundary and benchmark loop
1216:- prefer `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, `Critique delta ledger`, `Release promotion decision record`, and `Telemetry drift investigation memo` when the live control problem requires linked execution evidence rather than a summary verdict
1217-- do not let `Benchmark execution report`, `Replay suite verdict memo`, `Release evidence bundle v2`, or `Telemetry trend memo` imply a stronger controller or runner substrate than the evidence actually supports
1218:- if operational artifacts are absent, if only partial completion is visible, or if unresolved join failure blocks one gate, downgrade gate confidence before release, promotion, or drift escalation
1219:- keep `false-promotion`, `false-hold`, `drift-triggered review`, `partial completion`, and `unresolved join failure` as separately reviewable failure outcomes when promotion or monitoring decisions are being judged
1220-- let a newer compatible artifact supersede its stale predecessor explicitly rather than keeping both live by habit
1221-- before joining operational artifacts, check precedence, compatibility, freshness, and completeness; reject incompatible merges that would weaken a stronger artifact
1222-- preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in any joined artifact that survives release or telemetry review
1223-
